        },
        {
          "cont": [],
          "key": "description",
          "lead": [],
          "value": "\"bsc imprint — the WRITTEN half of knowing who the user is. `bsc ear` learns the maintainer's voice; this asks the same question of text, with no microphone and no camera: does this read like the person the app knows? A named feature vector over how someone writes — casing, apostrophes, habitual misspellings, emoticon vocabulary — accumulated from a corpus and reported PER DIMENSION. It decides nothing: no verdict, no score, and no record of any comparison, because a mechanism that accumulates evidence against a person is the one thing the maintainer's stated values forbid.\""
        }
      ],
